{"name":"Korila","hex":"#d7e9c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Cyclanthera pedata","blocks":[{"text":"Cyclanthera pedata, known as caigua, is a herbaceous vine grown for its edible fruit, which is predominantly used as a vegetable. It is known from cultivation only, and its use goes back many centuries as evidenced by ancient phytomorphic ceramics from Peru depicting the fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Cyclanthera_pedata_z02.JPG/330px-Cyclanthera_pedata_z02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclanthera_pedata","wikidata":"Q311101"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg/500px-Cyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg/1280px-Cyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg/500px-Cyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACyclanthera_pedata_kz01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Caihua.jpg/250px-Caihua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Caihua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Caihua.jpg/250px-Caihua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fruit in half showing seeds.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaihua.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wi